  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Peel the carrot, then shred using a julienne peeler or coarsely grate with a box grater. Separate the pak choy leaves. Combine the char siu sauce and 1 tbs white vinegar in a bowl and season with pepper. Crumble 1 stock cube into a heatproof jug, add 500ml (2 cups) boiling water and 1 tbs soy sauce and stir to dissolve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2279170/photos/large/127516_1-0df1d2f0b0430756d97754714d3401df.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook soup: Heat a drizzle of vegetable oil in a medium saucepan over medium-high heat. Cook the carrot, stirring, for 2 mins or until slightly softened. Add the stock and bring to the boil. Add the dumplings and cook for 2 mins. Add the pak choy and cook for a further 2 mins or until the dumplings are tender and the pak choy is wilted. Remove from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2279171/photos/large/127516_2-b711788234fc227b14ff3768b296cb13.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Taste the soup, then season with salt and pepper. Divide the dumpling soup among bowls. Drizzle with the char siu mixture, scatter with the sesame seeds and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2279172/photos/large/127516_3-f54bf79f106e04473b66785ae8597a99.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "...: How cool is that? Done in 15 minutes!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2279173/photos/large/127516_4-7e01b8bb446e283b437cf2ab55a85bfc.jpeg"
    },
